// `@sys` answers ambient facts about the process and the machine — the things a
// shell-adjacent script needs and `@env` has no business holding, because `@env`
// answers a record of *variables* and a working directory is not one.
//
// `os` and `arch` are the two that are the same on every run of a given build,
// so they are the two a fixture can assert. Both are effectful for the same
// reason the rest are: none of this is constant for the life of a run.
os ← ! @sys.os
arch ← ! @sys.arch
^ [os != "", arch != ""]
